<title>GERMANY: Dollar strength a &quot;normalisation&quot; - Germany's Stark.</title>
<headline>Dollar strength a &quot;normalisation&quot; - Germany's Stark.</headline>
<dateline>BAD NEUENAHR, Germany 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The recent rally in the dollar is a correction to the strength of the mark which prevailed in 1995 and 1995, Juergen Stark, state secretary at the German Finance Ministry, said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;In the dollar I see a normalisation of the strong overvaluation of the deutschemark in 1995/96,&quot; the Finance Ministry number two told a conference of German newspaper editors here.</p>
<p>The U.S. currency climbed after Stark's comment to a new 31-month high against the mark to stand at 1.6537/42 marks.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
